# This deployment's non-secret config, tracked in git. install.sh sources it
# AFTER /etc/forwarder/forwarder.env, so a key set here is owned by the repo:
# changing it is one reviewed commit on main, and CI redeploys the box. Keys
# not set here keep their box-local values. Secrets (FORWARDER_AGENT_TOKEN,
# WG_EDGE_PRIVKEY) are refused by install.sh — they never belong in git.

# UDP relay range for the OS-gallery WebTransport/QUIC media path (kernel-hive).
# UDP port = 54000 + registry slot, so this range is a cap on the public lineup.
# MUST equal ports.publicRelayLow-publicRelayHigh in kernel-hive's
# registry/registry-v1.json — its validator fails any tile outside the range,
# and this rule is what actually delivers the packets. History: while capped at
# 54130, slots 131+ were publicly dark yet healthy on the LAN (2026-08-09).
#
# Two windows live inside this one range:
#   54080-54255  production stations (54000 + slot). 54200 is the WebRTC
#                bridge's single ICE port, shared by every tile.
#   54256-54511  the walk-in clone pool, 256 ports of its own.
# The pool used to be carved out of the middle of station territory (slots
# 152-170) with live stations immediately above it, so growing the pool meant
# renumbering the fleet. Separate windows mean the two can never collide, and
# the 19 slots the pool vacates go back to the lineup.
UDP_RELAY_PORT_RANGE=54080-54511
